# Build context for the Node images, whose context is the REPO ROOT because pnpm
# workspaces resolve `workspace:*` deps through the root lockfile. That makes the
# context large by default, so what is excluded here matters more than usual.
#
# `services/ai` is not excluded wholesale: it has its own Dockerfile built from
# its own directory (ADR-0006 keeps it out of the pnpm graph), and nothing here
# needs it. Its virtualenv and model cache are the two directories that would
# dominate a context by themselves, so they are named explicitly.

node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/dist
coverage

services/ai/.venv
services/ai/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__

# Never send local credentials to the daemon. The one deliberate exception is
# apps/web/.env.local, which Next reads at BUILD time to inline the NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# values into the browser bundle; that file is documented as public-values-only
# and the web Dockerfile says so where it copies it.
.env
apps/api/.env
services/ai/.env

Octopus-Project-Plan.xlsx
